    "about": "Overview Swat Valley Tour: Malam Jabba, Miandam, Kalam &amp; Mahodand – 06 Days Explore the stunning beauty of Swat Valley with our 6-day tour . This journey takes you to the snowy slopes of Malam Jabba , the peaceful retreat of Miandam , and the vibrant Kalam Valley . Enjoy the serene waters of Mahodand Lake and immerse yourself in the rich culture of Swat, often called the “Switzerland of the East.” What to Expect: Malam Jabba: Enjoy thrilling skiing adventures and panoramic mountain views. Miandam: Relax in a quiet valley surrounded by lush greenery. Kalam Valley: Take in the breathtaking scenery and pleasant climate. Mahodand Lake: Visit this stunning alpine lake and enjoy its crystal-clear waters. Swat Valley: Experience a unique blend of natural beauty and cultural heritage. Why Choose This Tour? This tour is perfect for anyone looking to combine adventure and relaxation . With activities like skiing, sightseeing, and cultural exploration, you’ll experience the best of Swat Valley in just six days. Package Price: Affordable packages are available to fit different budgets. Whether you travel solo or with family, we guarantee a memorable experience. Book Your Adventure Today! Start your journey through the wonders of Swat Valley. Don’t miss this chance to explore one of Pakistan’s most scenic destinations. Reserve now and make memories that last a lifetime! &nbsp; Season Month Tour Start Date Price Per Person USD Minimum Travelers Required Spring Mid November &#8211; February Daily USD 780 1 Pax Winter March &#8211; May Daily USD 780 1 Pax Summer June &#8211; Mid September Daily USD 780 1 Pax Autumn Mid September &#8211; November Daily USD 780 1 Pax Book Your Swat Valley Adventure Today! Don’t miss out on this 6-day exploration of Swat Valley’s natural and cultural wonders. Whether you’re seeking adventure or tranquility, this tour has something for everyone. Reserve your spot now and create memories that will last a lifetime! &nbsp; &nbsp; Also Recommended: Ishkoman Valley Tour Follow us on Instagram: Safar Silsila",
